---
// Accessible parking placard (part of #393): the WV DMV's DMV-41-TR form as
// short lists. Every rule and fee is quoted in
// content/pdf-pages/wvdmv-accessible-parking.yaml.
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import FromPdf from '../components/FromPdf.astro';
import { pdfPage } from '../lib/pdf-pages.mjs';
import { telHref } from '../lib/content.mjs';
export const page = { door: "family", topic: "disability", label: "Accessible parking placard", summary: "Who can get a West Virginia handicap placard or plate, how to fill out the DMV form, where to mail it, and replacing a lost one" };
const d = pdfPage('wvdmv-accessible-parking');
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
const phone = '1-800-642-9066';
---
<Base title="Handicap parking placard in Mon County, WV: who qualifies and how to apply" description="How to get a West Virginia accessible parking placard or plate: the six conditions a medical provider can certify, how to fill out DMV form DMV-41-TR, where to mail it, temporary and permanent placards, and the $5.00 replacement, quoted from the form.">
  <h1>Accessible parking placard</h1>
  <p class="lede">You can read who qualifies below, then print the DMV form. You fill out the top, a medical provider fills out the bottom, and you mail it to the DMV. The rules are in a PDF form, so here they are as a short list. Questions: the form lists <a href={telHref(phone)}>{phone}</a>.</p>

  <nav aria-label="On this page">
    <ul>
      {d.sections.map((s) => <li><a href={`#${s.id}`}>{s.heading}</a></li>)}
    </ul>
  </nav>

  <FromPdf d={d} />

  <p>Where you can park with it in Morgantown, and paying at meters: see <a href={`${base}/parking/#accessible`}>parking in Morgantown</a>.</p>

  <p class="meta">This page is a reading aid. The DMV's form is the official version. Something wrong? <a href="https://github.com/david-shortman/mon-county-community-hub/issues/new?template=suggest-resource.yml">Tell us what is wrong on this page</a>.</p>
</Base>
